      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For Hiroshi, yes, leaning into a data-heavy, high-density interface focused on analytical tools is appropriate, aligning with a strong cultural preference for thoroughness and efficiency in decision-making. For Amara and Omar, a storytelling or outcome-oriented copy approach is highly effective; frame features around attainable goals and community-level financial security rather than just dense technical metrics. While archetypes help, remember that these are broad guidelines; the core strategy is balancing sophisticated functionality (for trust) with accessible language (for adoption) across all user groups.",
      "source": "target",
